  "id": "USN-8972-1",
  "summary": "haproxy vulnerabilities",
  "details": "It was discovered that HAProxy incorrectly handled truncated HTTP/2\nPING frames. A remote attacker could possibly use this issue to cause\nHAProxy to consume excessive CPU resources, leading to a denial of\nservice. (CVE-2026-110353)\n\nIt was discovered that HAProxy incorrectly handled certain HTTP/1.1\nchunked requests. A remote attacker could possibly use this issue to\ncause HAProxy to consume excessive CPU resources, leading to a denial\nof service. (CVE-2026-110354)",
